release_note = "0.20.0-2: upgraded to ConvertX 0.20.0 (latest upstream release); added the privacy policy (linked from Help) and a licence notice; fixed login over the NAS's plain-HTTP address (HTTP_ALLOWED) and closed registration after the first account; set a writable HOME so LibreOffice/Calibre conversions work as a non-root user; documented retention, user rights and the deletion channel; corrected the description. Rectified per review comments."
important    = "Open http://<NAS-IP>:8070/ on the LAN and create the first account immediately (registration closes after it), then log in. Cookies are allowed over plain HTTP so login works without HTTPS. Data and history stay in /Volume1/DockerAppData/convertxdocker/data; converted files are auto-deleted after 1 hour by default. Runs as uid 1000 with HOME=/home/convertx. Needs DockerEngine; use a registry mirror if Docker Hub is unreachable. No telemetry. Privacy policy: see the Help link."

